 "check": {
  "describe": "10:10:30 on Monday 2 November: the hour and minute hands make the classic V over a lit charcoal dial, the red second hand points straight down to six, MON 02 sits in the window at six, 7,412 steps fill three quarters of the green ring at nine and 82% fills the battery ring at three. battery-low (battery 15, 14:47:05 on Saturday 7 November, 12,500 steps): the battery ring is a short red arc with LOW under 15%, the steps ring is closed, SAT 07, the second hand points to one. sweep-1 and sweep-2, a quarter of a second apart, show the second hand between the seconds (it sweeps, it does not tick). mono-dark (always-on): black dial, grey batons, hollow white hands, no second hand, no gradient. Sizes 192, 300 and 454 are the same face scaled. light: a porcelain dial (white to pale grey), gunmetal faceted hands with soft grey shadows, black batons, deeper green, amber and red rings and a vermilion second hand; battery-low-light shows the red LOW ring on it.",
